{"name":"V05_persist6_reversal","hypothesis":"Groups whose V05 rose in fewer of the last 6 months will have higher returns next month, because persistent upward momentum in this average appears to be overpriced and later reverses, as submission 2's negative IC suggests.","falsified_if":"Mean cross-sectional rank IC of the negated feature is non-positive, or HAC t-statistic is below 1, in development data.","expression":"mult(persist(V05,6),-1)"}

Wait: mult(x,y) takes two variables, and -1 is not a variable, so that expression may be invalid. Here is a corrected version using only allowed operations:

{"name":"V05_yoy_tsz_reversal","hypothesis":"Groups whose V05 year-over-year change is unusually high relative to its own expanding history will have lower returns next month, because strong upward momentum in this average is overpriced and later reverses.","falsified_if":"Mean cross-sectional rank IC is non-negative, or HAC t-statistic is above -1, in development data.","expression":"tsz(yoy(V05),\"exp\")"}

